ch employee generates $29K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["StandardAero, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $9.1B market cap on $6.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $234M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.14\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.005130914580460344},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $9.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","